    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI extended the business-day rule in `BusinessDays.java` to roll past public holidays as well as weekends.\n\n**Change** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BusinessDays.java`):\n\n1. Added a pinned `HOLIDAYS` set \u2014 `2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28`.\n2. Extended `toBusinessDay(...)`'s roll-forward loop to also skip any date in that set, so when the adjusted date lands on a weekend *or* a listed holiday it advances one day at a time until it reaches a non-holiday weekday.\n\nThis keeps `BusinessDays` as the single source of truth, so every caller (`BuildOwner`, `CheckOwnerDailyLimit`, `FlagOwnerBulkSignup`, etc.) picks up the holiday rule automatically. The production set now matches the pinned `HOLIDAYS` the acceptance harness (`AcceptanceBase.toBusinessDay`) already assumes, and the test suite passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, BUILD SUCCESS).",
