    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean and idiomatic:\n\n- The new behavior lives in exactly the right unit: `toBusinessDay` was already the single roll-forward method, and the holiday skip is folded into its existing `while` loop rather than bolted on as a separate pass or duplicated into callers.\n- `HOLIDAYS` is a well-scoped `static final Set<LocalDate>` constant placed with the class it serves; `Set.of` + `contains` is the natural idiom for membership. Package-private visibility reasonably exposes it to tests without widening the API.\n- No duplication introduced and no class/method turning into a catch-all \u2014 `BusinessDays` remains a focused utility, and the change touches only the method and Javadoc the spec concerns.\n- Both the class-level and method-level Javadoc were updated to match the new semantics, which a maintainer here would expect.",
